Architecture plan for Issue #113: Rebrand product display name

Project shape:
- Rust Axum API in `crates/api`, shared domain/config/repositories in
  `crates/core`, and background jobs in `crates/worker`.
- React/Vite/Tailwind SPA in `web/`, with browser routes under
  `web/src/routes`, feature modules under `web/src/features`, and shell/provider
  wiring under `web/src/app`.
- Documentation and operational guidance live at the repository root
  (`README.md`, `PRODUCT.md`, `DEPLOY.md`) and seed/demo content lives under
  `scripts/` plus backend seed helpers.

Issue dependency:
- Issue #113 is independent. It is a public-facing copy rebrand only.

Implementation approach for #113:
- Search for externally visible uses of `ZeroClaw` and replace them with
  `Yet another Instagram` in UI text, browser metadata, email subject/body copy,
  Reels share copy, documentation, seed/demo content, and test fixtures.
- Keep internal identifiers unchanged: crate/package names, binary names,
  `SERVICE_NAME`, `REDIS_KEY_PREFIX`, `ZEROCLAW_SEED_CONFIRM`, deployment paths,
  systemd service names, Rust module names, and other operational identifiers.
- Validate with the existing Rust and web build path after copy changes.

Key decisions:
- Treat this as a text/content boundary change, not a rename of the codebase.
- Prefer targeted replacements in owned source/docs over broad mechanical renames
  that could alter internal identifiers.
- Preserve existing product behavior and data model; no database or API contract
  changes are expected.
